    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433-a1">

                <pb facs="0758" n="688" xml:id="pg688"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Señor Silva to Mr.
                        Dickinson</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">National Palace, Managua,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 13, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: According to the report received
                    to-day from the alcalde of Pueblo Grande of Ometepe, Castillo Viejo and Fort San
                    Carlos have been assaulted and taken by the enemies of the peace of Nicaragua;
                    and as it is certain that for this operation the revolutionists have made use of
                    some of the Transit Company’s steamers, his excellency the President has ordered
                    me to communicate this news to your excellency, and such as shall be hereafter
                    received, as I have the honor of doing, availing myself or the honor to assure
                    your excellency of the sentiments of esteem and respect with which I sign myself
                    your excellency’s very attentive and obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. SILVA.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. B. Dickinson, Minister Resident, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
